 "title": "Newton's method follows the tangent",
 "caption": "Newton's method replaces the curve by its tangent and solves that instead: x₁ = x₀ − f(x₀)/f′(x₀). From x₀ = 1 on f = x² − 2, the tangent meets zero at x₁ = 1 − (−1)/2 = 1.5; the next step gives 1.4167, already close to √2 = 1.41421.",
 "alt": "The parabola x squared minus 2 with its tangent at x = 1, which crosses the x-axis at 1.5, near the root at 1.414.",
 "description": [
  "f(1) = -1, f′(1) = 2.",
  "Tangent: y = -1 + 2(x − 1), zero at x = 1.5.",
  "Repeating: x₂ = 1.5 − 0.25/3 = 1.41667, x₃ = 1.41422.",
  "The number of correct digits roughly doubles each step."
